verified_identity; provenance.warnings records P4-10 identity confirmation and the CL-selected 134 S. Ct. 2473 identity is consistent with the record and ruling.\\\"}\\n{\\\"item\\\":4,\\\"target\\\":\\\"Heien v. North Carolina lake promotion and 574 U.S. 54 placement\\\",\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"CONFIRM\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"Status is verified_identity with promotion/cite-selector evidence in provenance.warnings; 574 U.S. 54 appears in citations.parallel and citations.all with whitelist source text, not as the selected official cite.\\\"}\\n{\\\"item\\\":4,\\\"target\\\":\\\"Arizona v. Youngblood lake promotion and date\\\",\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"CONFIRM\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"Status is verified_identity with promotion/date evidence in provenance.warnings; identity.date_decided is 1988-11-29 and identity.year is 1988.\\\"}\\n{\\\"item\\\":5,\\\"target\\\":\\\"Private and Foreign Searches hash-split edit\\\",\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"REFUTE\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"Lowers and Brillhart propositions match their stubs, no page-less wikilinks were introduced, and 'The Supreme Court has not resolved it' remains; however, both new bullets use unsanctioned labels 'Binding in-circuit (Nth Cir.); persuasive elsewhere' instead of the lexicon strings 'Binding in-circuit — Nth Cir.' and 'Persuasive (outside circuit)'.\\\"}\\n{\\\"item\\\":5,\\\"target\\\":\\\"Curtilage Eric Johnson edit\\\",\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"CONFIRM\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"The fact-bound common-hallway/no-curtilage proposition and preserved narrowness match the Eric Johnson stub; the label is 'Binding in-circuit — 4th Cir.' and the unpaged case is plain text with an opinion link.\\\"}\\n{\\\"item\\\":5,\\\"target\\\":\\\"Terry Stops Wilson edit\\\",\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"REFUTE\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"The main reasonable-suspicion proposition matches the Wilson stub and its label/link treatment is clean, but the added synthesis that firearm possession supplies no basis to disarm is not recorded in the stub's holding, which addresses